 		<Tag>TXT_KEY_CONCEPT_SAS_SEVOPEDIA_LEADER_LEGEND_PEDIA</Tag>
-		<English>[H1]Sevopedia Leader Legend[\H1][PARAGRAPH:2][H2]Attitude / Action Buttons[\H2][PARAGRAPH:2]- Attitude buttons row (top): pick the leader mood preview shown in the 3D leaderhead. Emoji mode uses icons (furious, annoyed, cautious, pleased, friendly); text mode uses FU/AN/CA/PL/FR.[PARAGRAPH:2]- Action buttons row (bottom): trigger animation preview (no/idle reset, greeting, agree, disagree) for the selected leader.[PARAGRAPH:2][H2]AI Personality Panel Legend[\H2][PARAGRAPH:2]- 1st column: "label", a shortened or full descriptive text, like/such as "T.W Likely" (a shortened explanation of what iMaxWarRand means ingame), as said earlier. This column contains the raw value too, for exhaustiveness, for example "T.W Likely (50)" for moctezuma, 50 is the raw value, or "T.W Likely (400)" for Gandhi, 400 is the raw value, for raw ai atributes. For aggregated ai aattributes, like contact probs, positive and negative memory resentments and affections, etc, the raw value is also displayed, but since there are many components (raw values) used to calculate the aggregated ai attribute, we instead display each of them "/" separated, for example for gandhi in the negative memory resentment category, the "D.W onFr (-200/120)" line shows that Gandhi has a raw ai attribute memory attitude percent of -200 (i.e. Gandhi resents quite strongly you declaring war on his friends) and a memory decay of 120. And for Moctezuma, for the same "D.W onFr" negative memory resentment, Moctezuma does not resent as much (memory attitude percent of -100, and memory decay same though of 120 (currently btw decays are same among all leaders (in civ4/advciv and thus advciv-sas too), not ideal but maybe functional))[PARAGRAPH:2]- 2nd column: the normalized score is displayed. As we explained before at the ranking calculation part, these scores are normalized, which means score is minimum 0 and maximum 100. Sometimes all leaders will have 50 (if same value among all leaders, happens sometimes in civ4 not ideal), and else leaders are ranked gradually from 0 (worse performer for better or worse) to 100 (best performer. Moctezuma performs good at war attributes, and gandhi good at peace attributes, for example). Note that this code is entirely dynamic, you can add more leaders and they'll get the new values and participate and possibly completely upset the best/worse performers ranking depending on their values (if they are different from current leaders ones, and how much), and you could also additionally tweak the existing leaders xml values. (If you think for example the roman leaders underperform in war, you may tweak their xml. As for aggregated ai attributes, they also display normalized scores, but since they are already normalized at their creation by definition, before leaders_data.py is (has finished being) generated), they are still displayed as normalized scores (min 0, max 100, unless all leaders have an equal score/value then all leaders get 50), but since they are already normalized, they are not re-normalized during caching and Sevopedia Leader computation. In short, they can be intepreted similarly as raw ai attributes.[PARAGRAPH:2]- (Inverted): when a line is marked (Inverted), lower raw values are better/more intense and higher raw values are weaker/less likely. Example: T.W Likely (getMaxWarRand) at 50 means much more war-prone than 400.[PARAGRAPH:2]- 3rd column: scale, this is an indicative display, raw ai attributes and aggregated ai attributes are graded graphically 10 by 10 with a symbol, but raw ai attributes use a "+" symbol, while ai aggregated symbols use a "#" symbol (trying to be visually clear while also civ4-compatible). So for example maxwarrand 400 gandhi has a score of 0 normalized among all leaders (it is highest score i.e Gandhi is the least war-like leader(s (if others have a value of 400 too))) so his scale is "++++++++++" (100th percentile), while moctezuma has a warrand of 50, score 100 among all leaders (very war-like (in a "T.W war Likely" way highest leader(s (if other have same value of 50)))), so his scale is "" (0th percentile). Aggregated ai attributes follow a similar logic, so for example for the contact offer probabilites ai aggregated attribute, shaka has a "Tr Tech (30/5)" score of 79, meanings he is likely, relatively to all leaders, to contact you for a tech trade offer, and 79th percentile is a bit short of 80 but still 7 scales/symbols so he will be "#######". If the value is 50 sharp, for raw ai attributes or ai aggregated attributes, the symbol will also be "+++++" or "#####". This is especially important because the last symbol is "=====", which only happens if, for both raw ai attributes and ai aggregated attributes, if all leaders have strictly the same raw value for this attribute aggregated or raw is same in this case functionally, i.e. they'll both get an equal scale symbol, and precisely 5 scales, also all leaders will scale 50. So 50 "+++++", 50 "#####", and 50 "=====" all have different meanings, one being respectively only for raw ai attributes scoring of said leader, the other of similarly same ai aggregated value of said leader, while the last being the display of an equal value among all leaders for an easier read.[PARAGRAPH:2][H2]Category Label -> Internal Key (Exhaustive, by category)[\H2][NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Core Personality:[NEWLINE]- Base Attitude -> getBaseAttitude.[NEWLINE]- Base Peace Weig -> getBasePeaceWeight.[NEWLINE]- Peace Weig Rand -> getPeaceWeightRand.[NEWLINE]- Worse Rank AC -> getWorseRankDifferenceAttitudeChange.[NEWLINE]- Better Rank AC -> getBetterRankDifferenceAttitudeChange.[NEWLINE]- Warmonger Resp -> getWarmongerRespect.[NEWLINE]- CloseBordSpark -> getCloseBordersAttitudeChange (Inverted).[NEWLINE]- Same Relig ACL -> getSameReligionAttitudeChangeLimit.[NEWLINE]- Diff Relig ACL -> getDifferentReligionAttitudeChangeLimit (Inverted).[NEWLINE]- Fav Civic ACL -> getFavoriteCivicAttitudeChangeLimit.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]BBAI Victory Weights:[NEWLINE]- Conquest -> getConquestVictoryWeight.[NEWLINE]- Domination -> getDominationVictoryWeight.[NEWLINE]- Culture -> getCultureVictoryWeight.[NEWLINE]- Diplomacy -> getDiplomacyVictoryWeight.[NEWLINE]- Space -> getSpaceVictoryWeight.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Flavors:[NEWLINE]- Military -> iFlavorMilitary.[NEWLINE]- Religion -> iFlavorReligion.[NEWLINE]- Production -> iFlavorProduction.[NEWLINE]- Gold -> iFlavorGold.[NEWLINE]- Science -> iFlavorScience.[NEWLINE]- Culture -> iFlavorCulture.[NEWLINE]- Growth -> iFlavorGrowth.[NEWLINE]- Espionage -> iFlavorEspionage.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]War Strategy:[NEWLINE]- T.W Likely -> getMaxWarRand (Inverted).[NEWLINE]- T.W NearPR -> getMaxWarNearbyPowerRatio.[NEWLINE]- T.W DistPR -> getMaxWarDistantPowerRatio.[NEWLINE]- T.W MinNearPR -> getMaxWarMinAdjacentLandPercent (Inverted).[NEWLINE]- Lim.W Likely -> getLimitedWarRand (Inverted).[NEWLINE]- Lim.W PR -> getLimitedWarPowerRatio.[NEWLINE]- Risky Aggr -> getBaseAttackOddsChange.[NEWLINE]- Risky AggrRand+ -> getAttackOddsChangeRand.[NEWLINE]- Raz C % -> getRazeCityProb.[NEWLINE]- TribRSneakW% -> getDemandRebukedSneakProb.[NEWLINE]- TribRef W% -> getDemandRebukedWarProb.[NEWLINE]- Dogpile Likely -> getDogpileWarRand (Inverted).[NEWLINE]- WAllianceMaker -> getDeclareWarTradeRand.[NEWLINE]- Share W ACL -> getShareWarAttitudeChangeLimit.[NEWLINE]- ResistCapitulPM -> getVassalPowerModifier.[NEWLINE]- Ref2TalkWSpan -> getRefuseToTalkWarThreshold.[NEWLINE]- MakePeaceLikely -> getMakePeaceRand (Inverted).[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Economic Preferences:[NEWLINE]- Max Gold Tr% -> getMaxGoldTradePercent.[NEWLINE]- Max GPT Tr% -> getMaxGoldPerTurnTradePercent.[NEWLINE]- NoTechYetRdy% -> getTechTradeKnownPercent.[NEWLINE]- NoTech2AdvT -> getNoTechTradeThreshold (Inverted).[NEWLINE]- Build Unit % -> getBuildUnitProb.[NEWLINE]- Wonder C.R -> getWonderConstructRand.[NEWLINE]- EspionageWeig -> getEspionageWeight.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Contact Offer Probabilities:[NEWLINE]- PeaceTreaty -> iAggregatedContactProbPeaceTreaty.[NEWLINE]- Open Borders -> iAggregatedContactProbOpenBorders.[NEWLINE]- Tr Map -> iAggregatedContactProbTradeMap.[NEWLINE]- Tr Tech -> iAggregatedContactProbTradeTech.[NEWLINE]- Tr Bonus -> iAggregatedContactProbTradeBonus.[NEWLINE]- Gave Help -> iAggregatedContactProbGiveHelp.[NEWLINE]- DefensPact -> iAggregatedContactProbDefensivePact.[NEWLINE]- PermAlliance -> iAggregatedContactProbPermanentAlliance.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Contact Demand Probabilities:[NEWLINE]- Relig Press -> iAggregatedContactProbReligionPressure.[NEWLINE]- Civic Press -> iAggregatedContactProbCivicPressure.[NEWLINE]- Stop Tr -> iAggregatedContactProbStopTrading.[NEWLINE]- Trib -> iAggregatedContactProbDemandTribute.[NEWLINE]- Help -> iAggregatedContactProbAskForHelp.[NEWLINE]- Join W -> iAggregatedContactProbJoinWar.[NEWLINE]- Contact probabilities raw pair shown in label: getContactRand(iContactType)/getContactDelay(iContactType).[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Refusal Thresholds (Offer):[NEWLINE]- Open Bord -> getOpenBordersRefuseAttitudeThreshold.[NEWLINE]- Map -> getMapRefuseAttitudeThreshold.[NEWLINE]- Tech -> getTechRefuseAttitudeThreshold.[NEWLINE]- Strategic Bonus -> getStrategicBonusRefuseAttitudeThreshold.[NEWLINE]- Happiness Bonus -> getHappinessBonusRefuseAttitudeThreshold.[NEWLINE]- Health Bonus -> getHealthBonusRefuseAttitudeThreshold.[NEWLINE]- PrideNoHelp -> getNoGiveHelpAttitudeThreshold.[NEWLINE]- DefensPact -> getDefensivePactRefuseAttitudeThreshold.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Refusal Thresholds (Demand):[NEWLINE]- Convert Religion -> getConvertReligionRefuseAttitudeThreshold.[NEWLINE]- Adopt Civic -> getAdoptCivicRefuseAttitudeThreshold.[NEWLINE]- D.W -> getDeclareWarRefuseAttitudeThreshold.[NEWLINE]- LoyaltyNoD.W -> getDeclareWarThemRefuseAttitudeThreshold (Inverted).[NEWLINE]- StopTr -> getStopTradingRefuseAttitudeThreshold.[NEWLINE]- LoyaltyNoStopTr -> getStopTradingThemRefuseAttitudeThreshold (Inverted).[NEWLINE]- ScaryNoTrib -> getDemandTributeAttitudeThreshold (Inverted).[NEWLINE]- C -> getCityRefuseAttitudeThreshold.[NEWLINE]- Native C -> getNativeCityRefuseAttitudeThreshold.[NEWLINE]- Vassal -> getVassalRefuseAttitudeThreshold.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]No War At:[NEWLINE]- Furious -> iNoWarAttitudeProbFurious.[NEWLINE]- Annoyed -> iNoWarAttitudeProbAnnoyed.[NEWLINE]- Cautious -> iNoWarAttitudeProbCautious.[NEWLINE]- Pleased -> iNoWarAttitudeProbPleased.[NEWLINE]- Friendly -> iNoWarAttitudeProbFriendly.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Attitude Changes:[NEWLINE]- Same Relig AC -> getSameReligionAttitudeChange.[NEWLINE]- Same Relig AD -> getSameReligionAttitudeDivisor.[NEWLINE]- Diff Relig AC -> getDifferentReligionAttitudeChange.[NEWLINE]- Diff Relig AD -> getDifferentReligionAttitudeDivisor.[NEWLINE]- Fav Civic AC -> getFavoriteCivicAttitudeChange.[NEWLINE]- Fav Civic AD -> getFavoriteCivicAttitudeDivisor.[NEWLINE]- Lost W AC -> getLostWarAttitudeChange.[NEWLINE]- At W AD -> getAtWarAttitudeDivisor.[NEWLINE]- At W ACL -> getAtWarAttitudeChangeLimit.[NEWLINE]- At Peace AD -> getAtPeaceAttitudeDivisor.[NEWLINE]- At Peace ACL -> getAtPeaceAttitudeChangeLimit.[NEWLINE]- Share W AC -> getShareWarAttitudeChange.[NEWLINE]- Share W AD -> getShareWarAttitudeDivisor.[NEWLINE]- Bonus Tr AD -> getBonusTradeAttitudeDivisor.[NEWLINE]- Bonus Tr ACL -> getBonusTradeAttitudeChangeLimit.[NEWLINE]- Open Bord AD -> getOpenBordersAttitudeDivisor.[NEWLINE]- Open Bord ACL -> getOpenBordersAttitudeChangeLimit.[NEWLINE]- Defens Pact AD -> getDefensivePactAttitudeDivisor.[NEWLINE]- Defens Pact ACL -> getDefensivePactAttitudeChangeLimit.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Misc Modifiers:[NEWLINE]- FreedomApprec -> getFreedomAppreciation.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Positive Memory Affections:[NEWLINE]- Gave Help -> iAggregatedPositiveMemoryGiveHelpAffection.[NEWLINE]- AcD -> iAggregatedPositiveMemoryAcceptDemandAffection.[NEWLINE]- AcRelig -> iAggregatedPositiveMemoryAcceptedReligionAffection.[NEWLINE]- AcCivic -> iAggregatedPositiveMemoryAcceptedCivicAffection.[NEWLINE]- AcJoin W -> iAggregatedPositiveMemoryAcceptedJoinWarAffection.[NEWLINE]- AcStop Tr -> iAggregatedPositiveMemoryAcceptedStopTradingAffection.[NEWLINE]- VotedForUs -> iAggregatedPositiveMemoryVotedForUsAffection.[NEWLINE]- Event Good -> iAggregatedPositiveMemoryEventGoodToUsAffection.[NEWLINE]- LiberatedC -> iAggregatedPositiveMemoryLiberatedCitiesAffection.[NEWLINE]- Indep -> iAggregatedPositiveMemoryIndependenceAffection.[NEWLINE]- Tr Tech -> iAggregatedPositiveMemoryTradedTechToUsAffection.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Negative Memory Resentments:[NEWLINE]- D.W -> iAggregatedNegativeMemoryDeclaredWarResentment.[NEWLINE]- D.W onFr -> iAggregatedNegativeMemoryDeclaredWarOnFriendResentment.[NEWLINE]- HirWAlly -> iAggregatedNegativeMemoryHiredWarAllyResentment.[NEWLINE]- Nuked Us -> iAggregatedNegativeMemoryNukedUsResentment.[NEWLINE]- Nuked Fr -> iAggregatedNegativeMemoryNukedFriendResentment.[NEWLINE]- RazC -> iAggregatedNegativeMemoryRazedCityResentment.[NEWLINE]- RazHolyC -> iAggregatedNegativeMemoryRazedHolyCityResentment.[NEWLINE]- Spy Caught -> iAggregatedNegativeMemorySpyCaughtResentment.[NEWLINE]- RefHelpUs -> iAggregatedNegativeMemoryRefusedHelpResentment.[NEWLINE]- Rej D -> iAggregatedNegativeMemoryRejectedDemandResentment.[NEWLINE]- Dn Relig -> iAggregatedNegativeMemoryDeniedReligionResentment.[NEWLINE]- Dn Civic -> iAggregatedNegativeMemoryDeniedCivicResentment.[NEWLINE]- Dn JoinW -> iAggregatedNegativeMemoryDeniedJoinWarResentment.[NEWLINE]- Dn StopTr -> iAggregatedNegativeMemoryDeniedStopTradingResentment.[NEWLINE]- StoppedTr -> iAggregatedNegativeMemoryStoppedTradingResentment.[NEWLINE]- TrEmbargo -> iAggregatedNegativeMemoryHiredTradeEmbargoResentment.[NEWLINE]- Made D -> iAggregatedNegativeMemoryMadeDemandResentment.[NEWLINE]- VotedAgUs -> iAggregatedNegativeMemoryVotedAgainstUsResentment.[NEWLINE]- Event Bad -> iAggregatedNegativeMemoryEventBadToUsResentment.[NEWLINE]- CancVassal -> iAggregatedNegativeMemoryCancelledVassalAgreementResentment.[NEWLINE]- Recent W -> iAggregatedNegativeMemoryDeclaredWarRecentResentment.